In each step, I will ask you to formalize a list of sentences. I will provide 
you with the context of the puzzle and the sentences to formalize. Your task is 
to formalize only these provided sentences into first-order logic using the 
structured output format specified. 

I will also provide you with a fixed set of predicates and constants that you 
can use in your formalization. Please make sure to be consistent with the 
provided predicates and constants. If you need to introduce new predicates or 
constants, you can do so, but do not new ones when there is already a suitable 
predicate or constant provided. Do not forget that you 
can still use builtin logical connectives and quantifiers and `Equals` as they 
are listed above, as needed.

Be in coherence with the provided previous formalizations! Use the same 
predicates and constants in a consistent way. If you think that the provided 
predicates and constants are sufficient, you can leave the `predicates` and 
`constants` sections in the structured output format as `None`, otherwise, add 
only the new predicates and constants that you need to the respective sections 
in the structured output format.